{{- /*
  Which kind of machine this is, detected from facts rather than prompted, so it
  can't be answered wrong and never goes stale:
    mac      my Macs (daily drivers)
    omarchy  Omarchy laptops (Arch + Hyprland desktop; ID=omarchy in os-release)
    server   every other Linux box: work devbox, homelab, throwaway VMs. Headless
             and reached over SSH from the Mac, which is why the xdg-open shim,
             $BROWSER and ssh-pty-resize belong here.
  Anything else (windows) falls through as its OS name.

  A partial instead of a value in chezmoi.toml so a machine that hasn't re-run
  `chezmoi init` still gets the right answer. Use it as:
    {{- $machine := includeTemplate "machine" . -}}
*/ -}}
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" -}}
mac
{{- else if eq (dig "osRelease" "id" "" .chezmoi) "omarchy" -}}
omarchy
{{- else if eq .chezmoi.os "linux" -}}
server
{{- else -}}
{{ .chezmoi.os }}
{{- end -}}
